From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:09:08 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 20/62] Plutonium: the box is where the window is; niri's
 resize cross-fade

Until the app answers a resize the page asked for (draws at any new size;
a terminal snaps to whole cells) or 300 ms pass, its latest frame is
stretched to the content box, as Hyprland draws a window it is resizing:
a page that snaps its layout, or a drag, shows no gap and no window
lagging behind the page. Then object-fit places what the app drew.

crossfade-easing eases the cross-fade (a CSS easing function; by default
close to niri's spring). A page animating the box with a FLIP from the
old size, started when the app answers with the same duration and easing,
gets niri's resize animation: size, stretched frames and their mix
together.

Only a box this element already showed the window in fades: attaching a
window, switching the element to another one, or showing an element that
was hidden or off screen doesn't. Resizes of 10 px or less don't fade.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
